{"abstract":"This paper presents the FactoryML framework that simplifies the deployment and integration of Machine Learning (ML) models in manufacturing factory environments. FactoryML facilitates packaging of ML models into a portable format and it facilitates the communication of deployed ML models in factory environments via Programmable Logic Controllers. In general FactoryML reduces the barrier to take learned models from a research and development side into an operational setting. The value of FactoryML has been demonstrated in a case study with a Danish company as well.","author_count":10,"contributors":["Wewer, Christian Remi","Mahapatra, Harshit","Esterle, Lukas","Larsen, Peter Gorm"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-772006"],"event":{"end":"2024-09-13","place":"Padova, it","start":"2024-09-10","title":"29th IEEE International Conference on Emerging Technologies and Factory Automation, ETFA 2024","year":"2024"},"filters":{"added":"2025-01","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","cluster_size":1,"corresponding_author":["Esterle, Lukas","Larsen, Peter Gorm","Wewer, Christian Remi"],"keyword":["Machine learning","Manufacturing","Open source"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-GTS","DI-U"],"level3":{"GTS":["DI-GTS-ALL","DI-GTS-ALX"],"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-AU"]},"level3all":["DI-GTS-ALX","DI-U-AU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"using factoryml for deployment of machine learning models in industrial production","src":["au"],"src-code":["DI-U-AU"],"type":"dcp","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"un","type":"url","url":"https://www.scopus.com/pages/publications/85207849014","version":"Other Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-772006","identifier":[{"id":"85207849014","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["au-2d97d7c0-52ad-4e91-9076-8d93dec21163"],"keyword":["MLOps","Machine Learning","manufacturing","open source"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-86127EA2F18924D5A9F2156A64C8A639"],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"au aarhus university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AU","l3nl":"Aarhus University","l3nn":"AU Aarhus University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AU Aarhus University","namevar":["Aarhus University, Technical Sciences, Department of Electrical and Computer Engineering, Department of Electrical and Computer Engineering - Signal Processing and Machine learning"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AU","used":1},{"affno":"2","key":"alexandra institute","l2":"DI-GTS","l2n":"GTS Institutes","l3":"DI-GTS-ALX","l3nn":"Alexandra Institute","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Alexandra Institute","namevar":["Alexandra Instituttet A/S"],"nora_code":"DI-GTS-ALX","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Christian Remi","key":"wewerpau","last":"Wewer","locid":"c4ea29b5-3b09-474b-8b97-1c0c390c5587","name":"Wewer, Christian Remi","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Harshit","key":"mahapatrapau","last":"Mahapatra","locid":"1cd54978-ea4d-4d30-8c49-a55527a510b8","name":"Mahapatra, Harshit","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Lukas","key":"esterlepau","last":"Esterle","locid":"c5e3910a-398e-472e-8773-dda31af63cc4","name":"Esterle, Lukas","orcid":"0000-0002-0248-1552","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Peter Gorm","key":"larsenpau","last":"Larsen","locid":"318d787b-3528-4a49-88be-60491de69409","name":"Larsen, Peter Gorm","orcid":"0000-0002-4589-1500","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Tullio","key":"facchinettipedh","last":"Facchinetti","name":"Facchinetti, Tullio","rank":5,"role":"Editor of Host Publication","rolecode":"pedh"},{"affno":"","first":"Angelo","key":"cenedesepedh","last":"Cenedese","name":"Cenedese, Angelo","rank":6,"role":"Editor of Host Publication","rolecode":"pedh"},{"affno":"","first":"Lucia Lo","key":"bellopedh","last":"Bello","name":"Bello, Lucia Lo","rank":7,"role":"Editor of Host Publication","rolecode":"pedh"},{"affno":"","first":"Stefano","key":"vitturipedh","last":"Vitturi","name":"Vitturi, Stefano","rank":8,"role":"Editor of Host Publication","rolecode":"pedh"},{"affno":"","first":"Thilo","key":"sauterpedh","last":"Sauter","name":"Sauter, Thilo","rank":9,"role":"Editor of Host Publication","rolecode":"pedh"},{"affno":"","first":"Federico","key":"tramarinpedh","last":"Tramarin","name":"Tramarin, Federico","rank":10,"role":"Editor of Host Publication","rolecode":"pedh"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.1109/etfa61755.2024.10710938","eisbn":["9798350361230"],"issn":["19460740"],"publisher":"Institute of Electrical and Electronics Engineers Inc.","series":"IEEE International Conference on Emerging Technologies and Factory Automation, ETFA","status":"p","title":"2024 IEEE 29th International Conference on Emerging Technologies and Factory Automation, ETFA 2024"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85207849014"],"search":{"DAF":["Aarhus University","All Danish Affiliations","All GTS Institutes","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-GTS","DI-GTS-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","GTS Institutes","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["au-2d97d7c0-52ad-4e91-9076-8d93dec21163"],"src":["AU Aarhus University"],"title":"Using FactoryML for Deployment of Machine Learning Models in Industrial Production","type":"Conference Paper","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-772006","year":"2024","yearsub":"2024"}
{"abstract":"Soluble alpha-amylases play an important role in the catabolism of polysaccharides. In this work, we show that the malt α -amylase can interact with the lipid membrane and further alter its mechanical properties. Vesicle fluctuation spectroscopy is used for quantitative measurement of the membrane bending rigidity of phosphatidylcholines lipid vesicles from the shape fluctuation based on the whole contour of Giant Unilamellar Vesicles (GUVs). The bending rigidity of the 1-palmitoyl-2-oleoyl-sn-glycero-3-phosphocholine lipid vesicles in water increases significantly with the presence of 0.14 micromolar alpha-amylase (AA) in the exterior solution. It appears that the enzyme present in the external solution interacts with the outer layer of the bilayer membrane, leading to an asymmetry of the solution on either side of the bilayer membrane and altering its elasticity. At AA concentration of 1.5 micromolars and above, changes in the morphology of the GUV membrane are observed. The interaction between AA in the external solution and the external leaflet causes the bilayer membrane to curve spontaneously, leading to the formation of outbuds, giving a positive spontaneous curvature of C0 ≤ 0.05 μm−1 at ≈ 1 mg / ml of the AA concentration. We validate and characterize its concentration-dependent role in stabilizing the membrane curvature. Our findings indicate that the involvement of the enzyme, depending on the concentration, can have a considerable effect on the mechanical characteristics of the membrane.","author_count":12,"contributors":["Kumar, Harshit","Mandal, Sayar","Yadav, Reena","Gupta, Suhasi","Meena, Hemraj","Kadu, Mayur","Kudawla, Rajni","Sharma, Pratibha","Kaur, Indu Pal","Maiti, Subhabrata","Ipsen, John Hjort","Bhatia, Tripta"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-723681"],"filters":{"added":"2024-03","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"11-50 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["Asia, South"],"corresponding_author":["Bhatia, Tripta"],"country":["India"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","Indian Institute of Science Education and Research Mohali","University Institute of Pharmaceutical Sciences"],"keyword":["Alpha amylase","Lipid protein interaction","Membrane mechanics"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-OT","DI-U"],"level3":{"OT":["Indian Institute of Science Education and Research Mohali"],"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-SDU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-SDU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"bottom up approach to explore alpha amylase assisted membrane remodelling","src":["sdu"],"src-code":["DI-U-SDU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"un","type":"url","url":"https://www.scopus.com/pages/publications/85182558260","version":"Other Version"},"funding_acknowledgement":["This research was carried out at the Indian Institute of Science Education and Research Mohali and is supported by the Ramalingaswami grant of DBT ( BT / RLF / Re-entry grant / 06/2020 ). H.K., S.G. and H.M. completed their Master’s degrees by writing the work in their theses. R.K. is currently working on her Ph.D. thesis. The authors declare that they have no competing interests."],"id":"S01-000.00-723681","identifier":[{"id":"38176612","type":"pmid"},{"id":"85182558260","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["sdu-dc117fbf-bd1e-4fa2-ba77-8fcb49b378a2"],"keyword":["Alpha amylase","Lipid Protein interaction","Membrane fluctuations","Membrane mechanics","Membrane rigidity"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-561B12DA74AA5C09283CDF9D239A714D"],"org":[{"affno":"1","country":"in","key":"indian institute of science education and research mohali","loc":["India","Asia, South"],"name":"Indian Institute of Science Education and Research Mohali","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"in","key":"university institute of pharmaceutical sciences","loc":["India","Asia, South"],"name":"University Institute of Pharmaceutical Sciences","used