{"abstract":"For the first time, we have used phase-contrast X-ray tomography to characterize the three-dimensional (3d) structure of cardiac tissue from patients who succumbed to Covid-19. By extending conventional histopathological examination by a third dimension, the delicate pathological changes of the vascular system of severe Covid-19 progressions can be analyzed, fully quantified and compared to other types of viral myocarditis and controls. To this end, cardiac samples with a cross section of 3.5 mm were scanned at a laboratory setup as well as at a parallel beam setup at a synchrotron radiation facility. The vascular network was segmented by a deep learning architecture suitable for 3d datasets (V-net), trained by sparse manual annotations. Pathological alterations of vessels, concerning the variation of diameters and the amount of small holes, were observed, indicative of elevated occurrence of intussusceptive angiogenesis, also confirmed by high resolution cone beam X-ray tomography and scanning electron microscopy. Furthermore, we implemented a fully automated analysis of the tissue structure in form of shape measures based on the structure tensor. The corresponding distributions show that the histopathology of Covid-19 differs from both influenza and typical coxsackie virus myocarditis.","author_count":11,"contributors":["Reichardt, Marius","Jensen, Patrick Møller","Dahl, Vedrana Andersen","Dahl, Anders Bjorholm","Ackermann, Maximilian","Shah, Harshit","Länger, Florian","Werlein, Christopher","Kuehnel, Mark P.","Jonigk, Danny","Salditt, Tim"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-328817"],"filters":{"added":"2022-03","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"11-50 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["Europe, EU","OECD"],"corresponding_author":["Jonigk, Danny","Salditt, Tim"],"country":["Germany"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","Georg-August-Universität Göttingen","Medizinische Hochschule Hannover","University Medical Center of Mainz"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-DTU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-DTU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"000000000003d virtual histopathology of cardiac tissue from covid 000000000019 patients based on phase contrast x ray tomography","src":["dtu"],"src-code":["DI-U-DTU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.7554/eLife.71359","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-328817","identifier":[{"id":"34930527","type":"pmid"},{"id":"85122136414","type":"scopus"},{"id":"PMC8747495","type":"pmcid"}],"ids":["dtu-5190b6e2-536a-4bdb-b0d1-7267240a6ac8"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-D18F2DAFEECF771323A286D20CA14391"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"loc","url":"https://backend.orbit.dtu.dk/ws/files/269593269/elife_71359_v2.pdf","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.7554/eLife.71359","version":"Published Version"}],"oai":{"class":"Realised","mra":["Science / Technology (SCI)"],"yearPub":"2021","yearSub":"2022"},"org":[{"affno":"1","country":"de","key":"georg august universität göttingen","loc":["Germany","Europe, EU","OECD"],"name":"Georg-August-Universität Göttingen","used":1},{"affno":"2","key":"dtu technical university of denmark","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-DTU","l3nl":"Technical University of Denmark","l3nn":"DTU Technical University of Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"DTU Technical University of Denmark","namevar":["Technical University of Denmark, Department of Applied Mathematics and Computer Science","Technical University of Denmark, Department of Applied Mathematics and Computer Science, Visual Computing"],"nora_code":"DI-U-DTU","used":1},{"affno":"3","country":"de","key":"university medical center of mainz","loc":["Germany","Europe, EU","OECD"],"name":"University Medical Center of Mainz","used":1},{"affno":"4","country":"de","key":"medizinische hochschule hannover","loc":["Germany","Europe, EU","OECD"],"name":"Medizinische Hochschule Hannover","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Marius","key":"reichardtmariuspau","last":"Reichardt","name":"Reichardt, Marius","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Patrick Moller","key":"jensenpatrickmøllerpau","last":"Jensen","locid":"7660ef3d-b946-4e63-bd11-a468381ada85","name":"Jensen, Patrick Møller","name_org":"Jensen, Patrick Moller","orcid":"0000-0002-8479-4885","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Vedrana Andersen","key":"dahlvedranaandersenpau","last":"Dahl","locid":"aced0c8f-957d-4bb3-9725-e410e42328f8","name":"Dahl, Vedrana Andersen","orcid":"0000-0001-6734-5570","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Anders Bjorholm","key":"dahlandersbjorholmpau","last":"Dahl","locid":"c2bad3c8-b172-481b-bb99-d3c2bc4004ef","name":"Dahl, Anders Bjorholm","orcid":"0000-0002-0068-8170","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3","corresponding":null,"first":"Maximilian","key":"ackermannmaximilianpau","last":"Ackermann","name":"Ackermann, Maximilian","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"4","corresponding":null,"first":"Harshit","key":"shahharshitpau","last":"Shah","name":"Shah, Harshit","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"4","corresponding":null,"first":"Florian","key":"längerflorianpau","last":"Länger","name":"Länger, Florian","rank":7,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"4","corresponding":null,"first":"Christopher","key":"werleinchristopherpau","last":"Werlein","name":"Werlein, Christopher","rank":8,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"4","corresponding":null,"first":"Mark P.","key":"kuehnelmarkppau","last":"Kuehnel","name":"Kuehnel, Mark P.","rank":9,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"4","corresponding":null,"first":"Danny","key":"jonigkdannypau","last":"Jonigk","name":"Jonigk, Danny","rank":10,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Tim","key":"salditttimpau","last":"Salditt","name":"Salditt, Tim","rank":11,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["34930527"],"pub":{"doi":"10.7554/elife.71359","issn":["2050084X"],"journal":"eLife","paperid":"e71359","publisher":"eLife Sciences Publications Ltd","publisher_org":"eLife Sciences Publications Ltd.","status":"p","title":"eLife","volume":"10"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85122136414"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Technical University of Denmark","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["dtu-5190b6e2-536a-4bdb-b0d1-7267240a6ac8"],"src":["DTU Technical University of Denmark"],"title":"3D virtual Histopathology of Cardiac Tissue from Covid-19 Patients based on Phase-Contrast X-ray Tomography","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-328817","year":"2021","yearsub":"2022"}
{"abstract":"BACKGROUND: Diagnostic tools for liver disease can now include estimation of the grade of hepatic steatosis (S0 to S3). Controlled attenuation parameter (CAP) is a non-invasive method for assessing hepatic steatosis that has become available for patients who are obese (FibroScan XL probe), but a consensus has not yet been reached regarding cutoffs and its diagnostic performance. We aimed to assess diagnostic properties and identify relevant covariates with use of an individual patient data meta-analysis. METHODS: We did an individual patient data meta-analysis, in which we searched PubMed and Web of Science for studies published from database inception until April 30, 2019. Studies reporting original biopsy-controlled data of CAP for non-invasive grading of steatosis were eligible. Probe recommendation was based on automated selection, manual assessment of skin-to-liver-capsule distance, and a body-mass index (BMI) criterion. Receiver operating characteristic methods and mixed models were used to assess diagnostic properties and covariates. Patients with non-alcoholic fatty liver disease (NAFLD) were analysed separately because they are the predominant patient group when using the XL probe. This study is registered with PROSPERO, CRD42018099284. FINDINGS: 16 studies reported histology-controlled CAP including the XL probe, and individual data from 13 papers and 2346 patients were included. Patients with a mean age of 46·5 years (SD 14·5) were recruited from 20 centres in nine countries. 2283 patients had data for BMI; 673 (29%) were normal weight (BMI <25 kg/m2), 530 (23%) were overweight (BMI ≥25 to <30 kg/m2), and 1080 (47%) were obese (BMI ≥30 kg/m2). 1277 (54%) patients had NAFLD, 474 (20%) had viral hepatitis, 285 (12%) had alcohol-associated liver disease, and 310 (13%) had other liver disease aetiologies. The XL probe was recommended in 1050 patients, 930 (89%) of whom had NAFLD; among the patients with NAFLD, the areas under the curve were 0·819 (95% CI 0·769-0·869) for S0 versus S1 to S3 and 0·754 (0·720-0·787) for S0 to S1 versus S2 to S3. CAP values were independently affected by aetiology, diabetes, BMI, aspartate aminotransferase, and sex. Optimal cutoffs differed substantially across aetiologies. Risk of bias according to QUADAS-2 was low. INTERPRETATION: CAP cutoffs varied according to cause, and can effectively recognise significant steatosis in patients with viral hepatitis. CAP cannot grade steatosis in patients with NAFLD adequately, but its value in a NAFLD screening setting needs to be studied, ideally with methods beyond the traditional histological reference standard. FUNDING: The German Federal Ministry of Education and Research and Echosens.","author_count":32,"contributors":["Petroff, David","Blank, Valentin","Newsome, Philip N","Shalimar, no-firstname","Voican, Cosmin Sebastian","Thiele, Maja","de Lédinghen, Victor","Baumeler, Stephan","Chan, Wah Kheong","Perlemuter, Gabriel","Cardoso, Ana-Carolina","Aggarwal, Sandeep","Sasso, Magali","Eddowes, Peter J","Allison, Michael","Tsochatzis, Emmanuel","Anstee, Quentin M","Sheridan, David","Cobbold, Jeremy F","Naveau, Sylvie","Lupsor-Platon, Monica","Mueller, Sebastian","Krag, Aleksander","Irles-Depe, Marie","Semela, David","Wong, Grace Lai-Hung","Wong, Vincent Wai-Sun","Villela-Nogueira, Cristiane A","Garg, Harshit","Chazouillères, Olivier","Wiegand, Johannes","Karlas, Thomas"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-639301"],"filters":{"added":"2021-10","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"11-50 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["America, South","Asia, East","Asia, South","Europe, EU","Europe, Non-EU","OECD"],"corresponding_author":["Karlas, Thomas"],"country":["Brazil","China","France","Germany","India","Malaysia","Romania","Switzerland","United Kingdom"],"glorg":["Addenbrooke's Hospital","All Global Affiliations","All India Institute of Medical Sciences","Angelika Lautenschläger Children's Hospital","Cambridge University Hospitals NHS Foundation T