g the M and XL probes : an individual patient data meta-analysis","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-639301","year":"2021","yearsub":"2021"}
{"abstract":"Flexible and controllable self-regulating heating devices with positive temperature coefficient (PTC) behaviour are potentially excellent candidates in applications like healthcare, soft robotics, artificial skin and wearable electronics. Although extensive studies have been carried out in this field to understand the mechanism of PTC effect, rather limited conclusions have been reached. Many controversies remain on the dominating factors that influence the PTC performance of composites, hence limiting their design and broader applications. Herein, we propose a systematic study to explore the PTC phenomenon and the underlying mechanism, from a conductive network viewpoint, taking account of both conductive fillers and polymer matrices. Three representative conductive fillers with distinct dimensions and shapes (0D silver coated glass spheres, 1D carbon nanotubes and 2D graphene nanoplatelets), in combination with three different polymer matrices (high density polyethylene, thermoplastic polyurethane and polycarbonate) were selected to elucidate the effect of the “robustness” of different conductive networks on PTC behaviour in conductive polymer composites (CPCs). The desired conductive network can be obtained by selecting preferentially larger filler size, lower filler aspect ratio and/or selective distribution of filler (e.g. in the amorphous region of semi-crystalline polymers). The highest PTC intensity was observed around the “critical” percolation threshold, in correspondence of networks with the lowest number of inter-particle contacts. This study can serve as a guideline in the selection of the most appropriate conductive filler and polymer matrix for various self-regulating heating requirements and final applications.","author_count":11,"contributors":["Liu, Yi","Asare, Eric","Porwal, Harshit","Barbieri, Ettore","Goutianos, Stergios","Evans, Jamie","Newton, Mark","Busfield, James J.C.","Peijs, Ton","Zhang, Han","Bilotti, Emiliano"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-308996"],"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"11-50 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["Asia, East","Europe, Non-EU","OECD"],"corresponding_author":["Liu, Yi"],"country":["Japan","United Kingdom"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","Japan Agency for Marine-Earth Science and Technology","LMK Thermosafe Ltd.","Queen Mary University of London","University of Warwick"],"keyword":["Carbon nanotube CNT","Nanocomposites"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-DTU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-DTU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"the effect of conductive network on positive temperature coefficient behaviour in conductive polymer composites","src":["dtu"],"src-code":["DI-U-DTU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://backend.orbit.dtu.dk/ws/files/269597763/The_Effect_of_Conductive_Network_on_Positive_Temperature_Coefficient_Behaviour_in_Conductive_Polymer_Composites_For_repository.pdf","version":"Pre-print"},"id":"S01-000.00-308996","identifier":[{"id":"85090971589","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["dtu-0eab9c65-950d-4f38-85fe-7e4a4f1081b2"],"keyword":["Carbon nanotube (CNT)","Graphene nanoplatelet (GNP)","Nanocomposites","Pyroresistitivity"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-AF5E6F27C3B8CD9535EE26CB9B7FC73E"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://backend.orbit.dtu.dk/ws/files/269597763/The_Effect_of_Conductive_Network_on_Positive_Temperature_Coefficient_Behaviour_in_Conductive_Polymer_Composites_For_repository.pdf","version":"Pre-print"}],"oai":{"class":"Realised","mra":["Science / Technology (SCI)"],"yearPub":"2020","yearSub":"2020"},"org":[{"affno":"1","country":"gb","key":"queen mary university of london","loc":["United Kingdom","Europe, Non-EU","OECD"],"name":"Queen Mary University of London","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"gb","key":"lmk thermosafe ltd","loc":["United Kingdom","Europe, Non-EU","OECD"],"name":"LMK Thermosafe Ltd.","used":1},{"affno":"3","country":"jp","key":"japan agency for marine earth science and technology","loc":["Japan","Asia, East","OECD"],"name":"Japan Agency for Marine-Earth Science and Technology","used":1},{"affno":"4","key":"dtu technical university of denmark","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-DTU","l3nl":"Technical University of Denmark","l3nn":"DTU Technical University of Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"DTU Technical University of Denmark","namevar":["Technical University of Denmark, Department of Wind Energy","Technical University of Denmark, Department of Wind Energy, Composite Mechanics and Structures"],"nora_code":"DI-U-DTU","used":1},{"affno":"5","country":"gb","key":"university of warwick","loc":["United Kingdom","Europe, Non-EU","OECD"],"name":"University of Warwick","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Yi","key":"liupau","last":"Liu","name":"Liu, Yi","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Eric","key":"asarepau","last":"Asare","name":"Asare, Eric","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Harshit","key":"porwalpau","last":"Porwal","name":"Porwal, Harshit","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3","corresponding":null,"first":"Ettore","key":"barbieripau","last":"Barbieri","name":"Barbieri, Ettore","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"4","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Stergios","key":"goutianospau","last":"Goutianos","locid":"0958ded5-b7aa-4df2-9a8e-d35b1ba77fdc","name":"Goutianos, Stergios","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Jamie","key":"evanspau","last":"Evans","name":"Evans, Jamie","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Mark","key":"newtonpau","last":"Newton","name":"Newton, Mark","rank":7,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"James J.C.","key":"busfieldpau","last":"Busfield","name":"Busfield, James J.C.","rank":8,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"5","corresponding":null,"first":"Ton","key":"peijspau","last":"Peijs","name":"Peijs, Ton","rank":9,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Han","key":"zhangpau","last":"Zhang","name":"Zhang, Han","rank":10,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Emiliano","key":"bilottipau","last":"Bilotti","name":"Bilotti, Emiliano","rank":11,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.1016/j.compositesa.2020.106074","issn":["1359835X"],"journal":"Composites Part A: Applied Science and Manufacturing","paperid":"106074","publisher":"Elsevier","status":"p","title":"Composites Part A: Applied Science and Manufacturing","volume":"139"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85090971589"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Technical University of Denmark","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["dtu-0eab9c65-950d-4f38-85fe-7e4a4f1081b2"],"src":["DTU Technical University of Denmark"],"title":"The effect of conductive network on positive temperature coefficient behaviour in conductive polymer composites","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-308996","year":"2020","yearsub":"2020"}
{"abstract":"Thirty-eight mutants of RNase Sa (ribonuclease from Streptomyces aureofaciens) were examined for their structure, thermal sensitivity, and tendency to aggregate. Although a biphasic correlation was seen between the effect of temperature on structure and the free energy of transfer changes in many of the mutants, little correlation was seen between the time at which aggregation is initiated or the rate of aggregation and the thermal sensitivity of the mutants. It is hypothesized that the nature of contacts between protein molecules in the associated (aggregated) phase rather than structural changes dominates the aggregation process for these series of mutants.","author_count":7,"contributors":["Khasa, Harshit","Kramer, Ryan","Maddux, Nathan","Hamborg, Mette","Joshi, Sangeeta B","Volkin, David B","Middaugh, C Russell"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-458524"],"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["No Matches Found"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","cluster_size":1,"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-OT"],"level3":{"OT":["Department of Pharmaceutical Chemistry, Macromolecule and Vaccine Stability Center, University of Kansas, Lawrence, Kansas, 66047."]},"level3all":[]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"studies of the aggregation of rnase sa","src":["ku"],"src-code":["DI-U-KU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1002/jps.23841","version":"Other Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-458524","identifier":[{"id":"84895928159","type":"scopus"},{"id":"24382748","type":"pmid"}],"ids":["ku-6cfb8904-c10d-442b-86e2-724cfd99e465"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-3-3C65D14CD0E23AD4EF55BBC5F8648D4F"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1002/jps.23841","version":"Other Version"}],"oai":{"class":"Unused","mra":["Medicine (MED)"],"yearPub":"2014","yearSub":"2014"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"miscellaneous","l2":"DI-OT","l2n":"Miscellaneous","l3":"DI-OT","l3nl":"Other Research","l3nn":"Miscellaneous","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Miscellaneous","namevar":["Department of Pharmaceutical Chemistry, Macromolecule and Vaccine Stability Center, University of Kansas, Lawrence, Kansas, 66047."],"nora_code":"DI-OT","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","first":"Harshit","key":"khasapau","last":"Khasa","name":"Khasa, Harshit","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Ryan","key":"kramerpau","last":"Kramer","name":"Kramer, Ryan","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Nathan","key":"madduxpau","last":"Maddux","name":"Maddux, Nathan","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Mette","key":"hamborgpau","last":"Hamborg","locid":"60033447-ae12-47fb-bd95-91414adeb321","name":"Hamborg, Mette","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Sangeeta B","key":"joshipau","last":"Joshi","name":"Joshi, Sangeeta B","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"David B","key":"volkinpau","last":"Volkin","name":"Volkin, David B","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"C Russell","key":"middaughpau","last":"Middaugh","name":"Middaugh, C Russell","rank":7,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["24382748"],"pub":{"doi":"10.1002/jps.23841","issn":["00223549","15206017"],"issue":"2","journal":"Journal of Pharmaceutical Sciences","pages":"395-9","status":"p","title":"Journal of Pharmaceutical Sciences","volume":"103"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Miscellaneous","DI-ALL","DI-OT","DI-OT-ALL","Miscellaneous","Other Research"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["ku-6cfb8904-c10d-442b-86e2-724cfd99e465"],"src":["KU University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Studies of the aggregation of RNase Sa","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-458524","year":"2014","yearsub":"2014"}
